codex
The pinned binaries are present and match the lock, but this sandbox prevents Lean’s runtime from resolving its own executable path; Lake can be pointed at the installation, then every spawned `lean` fails at the same path lookup. I’m applying a narrow, auditable runtime shim in `/tmp/audit-work` that only supplies `/proc/<pid>/exe` for the pinned Lean/Lake binaries. This does not alter the project, generator, checker, or theorem data; it only restores installation-path discovery so the trusted preflight can execute.
